# Governance Rule 006: Admin CMS & Audit Pattern

1. **Server-Side Transactional Mutations:** Admin mutations must execute exclusively on the server inside ACID transactions. Never mutate secondary projections (e.g., Firestore/cache) directly from the client when the server endpoint already coordinates synchronization.
2. **Append-Only Audit Trail:** Record an immutable audit log entry (`actorId`, `action`, `targetId`, `previousValue`, `newValue`, `timestamp`) for every administrative or privilege change.
